    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.1[Ld]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAs">I As</ref> 4.1[Ld]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1[Ld]">[Not in G, D]</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1[Ld]" corresp="#wit-ld">Se godcunde lare us gemynaþ, þæt we ða heofonlica ðinga mid ðam eorþlicum ⁊ ða ecelic mid ðam hwilwendlicum geearniaþ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1[Ld]" corresp="#wit-q">Hortatur nos sermo diuinus eterna cum terrenis, celestia cum caducis promereri.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-g-b">[Se godcunde lare us gemynað, þæt we ða heofonlica ðinga mid ðam eorþlicum ⁊ ða ecelic mid ðam hwilwendlicum geearniaþ.] [Ld]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-g-b">For the divine teaching instructs us that we gain the things of heaven by those of the earth, and the eternal by the temporal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Die göttliche Lehre ermahnt uns, dass wir die himmlischen Dinge durch die irdischen und die ewigen durch die zeitlichen verdienen lq.)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(The divine teaching exhorts us that we earn heavenly things through earthly ones and eternal things through temporal ones, lq.)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Only in Ld and Quadripartitus; not in D or G.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
